00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.350
Leah: Let's hear about the importance of
productive feedback in the scrum process.

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:15.940
Alex: I think that's such a key
element of the whole scrum process

00:00:15.969 --> 00:00:20.930
is that that rapid feedback loop
that you're only kind of committing

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:22.970
to a small amount of work at a time.

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:25.590
And at the end of every sprint you are...

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:32.169
you're having a kind of sprint review,
you're demoing the product ideally to

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:35.849
the key stakeholders, ideally to the
end users or the customers, and you're

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:41.970
getting that feedback that rapid feedback
incorporating that back into the process

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:47.099
so that you can then work out what to
do differently for the next sprint and

00:00:47.099 --> 00:00:49.260
how you can then evolve the product.

00:00:52.869 --> 00:00:56.150
I would say it's important
throughout the whole process.

00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:02.820
Quite specifically at the sprint reviews,
that's a great time for the team to kind

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:07.590
of demo the work that they've done for
the previous sprint and get that that

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:14.750
fast feedback from the stakeholders, from
the end users Also for the core scrum

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:20.040
team themselves at the retrospectives
to kind of review what went well, what

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:22.330
didn't go well, any kind of learnings.

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:27.250
And then again, incorporating
that into into the next sprint.

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:30.430
Just as part of that continuous
learning cycle, really.

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:37.160
Feedback can be given in a
variety of different ways.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:41.789
And I think throughout the whole process
is it's important to get that feedback.

00:01:42.059 --> 00:01:46.620
Again, going back to the key
sprint ceremonies, at the sprint

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:49.320
reviews, at the retrospectives.

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:53.220
Making sure you're giving kind of peer
feedback, peer review and feedback

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:54.580
throughout the process as well.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:59.310
We do obviously hold daily scrums
every day, just to 15 minutes with

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:03.189
the core scrum team, for them to
talk about, you know, what they

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:06.049
did yesterday, what they're doing
